    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "fb618c77_9df749ea",
        "filename": "internal/wycheproof/dsa_test.go",
        "patchSetId": 8
      },
      "lineNbr": 110,
      "author": {
        "id": 28759
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-12-04T17:27:14Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Done\n\nI actually think that commenting on falses is even more important that commenting on trues, because it\u0027s saying that \"this case is acceptable by many implementations, but we are specifically not going to allow it because of X reason\".",
      "parentUuid": "dd5d8e84_7fa06f29",
      "revId": "f3e003d2489733f204fbbdc38d75be1067803db5",
      "serverId": "62eb7196-b449-3ce5-99f1-c037f21e1705",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "f70b039c_e20bf368",
        "filename": "internal/wycheproof/dsa_test.go",
        "patchSetId": 8
      },
      "lineNbr": 110,
      "author": {
        "id": 11715
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-12-04T20:31:34Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "More comments the better. Trues are important here because accepting an invalid signature is a security vulnerability, while rejecting a valid one is just a bug.\n\nIn general Go aims to be strict about everything we can get away with, so ideally we\u0027d want all entries to be falses.",
      "parentUuid": "fb618c77_9df749ea",
      "revId": "f3e003d2489733f204fbbdc38d75be1067803db5",
      "serverId": "62eb7196-b449-3ce5-99f1-c037f21e1705",
